+# This script resets the VAP (Virtual Access Point) UCI configuration for the
+# wireless interface. It is invoked during the DEV_RESET_DEFAULT flow from the
+# prplmesh application.
+#
+# The whole wireless config is (re)built ONLY through UCI commands (no direct
+# file writes). Per radio it writes exactly one AP VAP (SSID "OpenWrt") and one
+# STA (backhaul) VAP, with the SAME options the application would write:
+#
+#   AP VAP (wlan<band>.1):
+#     device, network=lan, mode=ap, ssid=OpenWrt
+#     2.4/5 GHz -> encryption=none
+#     6 GHz     -> encryption=sae, sae_pwe=1, key=0123456789 (open BSS not allowed on 6 GHz)
+#     5 GHz     -> additionally wps_pushbutton=1, multi_ap=2 (fronthaul+backhaul combined AP)
+#
+#   STA VAP (wlan<band>):
+#     device, network=lan, mode=sta, wps_pushbutton=1, multi_ap=1, wds=1
+#
+# htmode handling (per band, mirroring bpl_cfg_reset_ap_vaps_to_default):
+#   - If the radio's CURRENT htmode is EHT* (Wi-Fi 7 / 11be) -> keep it EHT<width> (11be).
+#   - Otherwise (HE/VHT/HT/empty)                            -> bring it up as HE<width> (11ax).
+#   The channel-width suffix is preserved from the existing htmode. HE has no
+#   320 MHz, so a 320 width is clamped to 160 for the HE family; when the width
+#   cannot be determined it defaults to 80.
+#
+# After committing the UCI, it invokes the bare "wifi" (full reconfigure) so
+# netifd regenerates hostapd/wpa_supplicant configs and brings the radios up.
 
 # Detect the OS type from uname -a output
 UNAME_OUTPUT=$(uname -a)
@@ -19,112 +42,182 @@ fi
 
